  <h2>Short description (25 words)</h2>
  <p>Whoships puts your GitHub organization on your Mac desktop: pull requests waiting for you, red CI with the reason, DORA metrics and security alerts, in widgets.</p>

  <h2>Long description</h2>
  <p>Engineering leads keep twenty browser tabs open to know what is going on in their GitHub organization. Whoships replaces them with ten watchers that live on the Mac desktop. Needs me lists the reviews waiting for you and your pull requests with failed CI, with the reason worked out from the job log. Attention flags red CI on main, force pushes and unreviewed merges across the organization. Flow health, Delivery (DORA), Security and CI health give team leads and CTOs cycle time, the four DORA metrics, Dependabot and code scanning alerts, and flaky workflows.</p>
  <p>Everything shows in widgets from small to extra large, a menu bar count, and a dashboard that sits on the wallpaper behind your windows. Whoships reads GitHub directly from the Mac, read-only, with no server in between. It can be tried with sample data and no account, is free for 14 days with your own organization, and then costs a one-time €{{ site.price.eur }}.</p>

